{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.95.030","page_type":"section"},"citation":"5.95.030","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.95.030","content_hash":"54dc76ffd328e1ddb6317f1c58100d6af5e991cb98fed8c76aa2f1dff3d694fa","heading":"Craftsmen applications.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.95.030:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.95.030","text":"(a) Applications for examination for a master mobile home craftsman license, a journeyman mobile home craftsman license, or an apprentice mobile home craftsman license shall be made to the Mobile Home Craftsmen Board of Examiners. The Board shall examine the applicant, shall consider such applicant’s experience, training and other qualifications and, upon successful passage of the examination, shall issue the license for which application was made. The minimum qualifications shall be the same as are set out in this chapter.\n(b) Fees under this section shall be as follows:\n(1) | Generally. |\n| (i) | Contractor | $250.00\n| (ii) | Master | None\n| (iii) | Journeyman | None\n| (iv) | Apprentice registration | $4.00\n(2) | Renewal of License. |\n| (i) | Contractor | $50.00\n| (ii) | Master | $50.00\n| (iii) | Journeyman | $15.00\n| (iv) | Apprentice registration | $4.00\n(3) | Registration for Out-of-City Licenses. |\n| (i) | Master | $50.00\n| (ii) | Journeyman | $15.00\n(1)\nGenerally.\n(i)\nContractor\n$250.00\n(ii)\nMaster\nNone\n(iii)\nJourneyman\nNone\n(iv)\nApprentice registration\n$4.00\n(2)\nRenewal of License.\n(i)\nContractor\n$50.00\n(ii)\nMaster\n$50.00\n(iii)\nJourneyman\n$15.00\n(iv)\nApprentice registration\n$4.00\n(3)\nRegistration for Out-of-City Licenses.\n(i)\nMaster\n$50.00\n(ii)\nJourneyman\n$15.00\n(c) All licenses and registrations shall expire December 15th. All licenses may be renewed for a period of 90 days after expiration. Failure to renew within such 90-day period shall cause the license to be null and void. Thereafter, renewal of license shall be considered and treated as an application for a new license and subject to all applicable provisions therefor. (Code 1981 § 25-162. Code 1995 § 98-223.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"cbecb575-a1f7-58f0-94ba-58c93cb6964a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.95.030","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.95.030","content_hash":"26f776c546c1e47cbde700a7d289576341ac7c9a6a3381fd033d26e22c247fdd","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.95.030:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.95.030:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.95.030","text":"(a) Applications for examination for a master mobile home craftsman license, a journeyman mobile home craftsman license, or an apprentice mobile home craftsman license shall be made to the Mobile Home Craftsmen Board of Examiners. The Board shall examine the applicant, shall consider such applicant’s experience, training and other qualifications and, upon successful passage of the examination, shall issue the license for which application was made. The minimum qualifications shall be the same as are set out in this chapter.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"1b584ffe-129e-5948-adf4-21d425113bee"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.95.030","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.95.030","content_hash":"0a2c0a69963e58dff7f0a9f81202a11b28e789c824e4f22b9a41aff9303809c0","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.95.030:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka: